                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle i^\ast, j^\ast \rangle \colon O(X) \to O(U) \times O(K)
              is identified with the comonadic functor attached to the comonad (2). In particular,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
